{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  Section: Customer login (sign-in page, /account/login)
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Shopify's sign-in page, in the same design as the sign-in popup:
  the card from snippets/global-account-forms.liquid, starting on "Sign in".
  The "Create account" tab and "Forgot password?" switch views in place.

      ┌──────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┐
      │ dark panel   │ [ Sign in | Create account ]    │
      │              │ Welcome back                    │
      │              │ Email / Password / [SIGN IN →]  │
      └──────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘
                 Just here to check out? [Continue as guest]   ← only from checkout

  - Failed sign-ins / password resets come back to this page; the card shows
    Shopify's messages (and opens on "Reset your password" after a reset).
  - "Continue as guest": only when the shopper came from checkout and the
    store allows guest checkout (shop.checkout.guest_login).

  Used in:   templates/customers/login.json
  Snippets:  snippets/global-account-forms.liquid (+ panel, field)
  CSS:       assets/global-account.css (classes .account-page, .account-card*)
  JS:        assets/global-account.js (views, password toggle, #recover)
  Text:      locales → customer.*
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="page-width account-page">
  {% render 'global-account-forms', context: 'page', view: 'login' %}

  {%- comment -%} Guest checkout (Shopify shows this option only when coming from checkout) {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if shop.checkout.guest_login -%}
    <div class="account-guest">
      <p>{{ 'customer.login.guest_text' | t }}</p>
      {%- form 'guest_login' -%}
        <button type="submit" class="button button--outline button--sm account-guest__button">{{ 'customer.login.guest_button' | t }}</button>
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Schema (theme editor settings) — JSON cannot contain comments, so they live here.
  No section settings: the side panel is set in Theme settings > Customer accounts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Customer login",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-customer-login",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["customers/login"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Side panel image, heading, text and perks: Theme settings > Customer accounts."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
